WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:19.983
"Bye, Mom." Nina hugged her mother.

2
00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:25.169
They had walked together to Kids Central Summer Camp today.

3
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:31.968
"Bye, sweetie. I'll be back with Aunt Sujong at three o'clock to pick you up," Nina's mom said.

4
00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:39.949
"Yay!" Nina's Aunt Sujong was arriving from Korea today.

5
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:43.865
She was going to stay at Nina's house for one week.

6
00:00:43.866 --> 00:00:46.311
"I hope we make a craft today.

7
00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:51.106
Then I can give it to Aunt Sujong," Nina thought.

8
00:00:51.107 --> 00:00:55.514
In the gym Mr. Dunn was holding a box of strawberries.

9
00:00:55.515 --> 00:00:59.358
Izzie was trying to guess how many strawberries were in it.

10
00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:04.249
"Twenty-two," Izzie said. "I bet there are twenty-two."

11
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.891
"What do you think, Nina?" Mr. Dunn asked.

12
00:01:07.892 --> 00:01:10.355
Nina looked in the box.

13
00:01:10.356 --> 00:01:14.622
"Are we making food today?" she asked, disappointed.

14
00:01:14.623 --> 00:01:16.982
"We're not making a craft?"

15
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:20.590
"We're making smoothies!" Jason guessed.

16
00:01:20.591 --> 00:01:26.260
"Nope. But you'll like this too," Mr. Dunn said.

17
00:01:26.261 --> 00:01:30.955
"We're making strawberry jam," Mr. Dunn said.

18
00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:34.195
"Have any of you made jam before?"

19
00:01:34.196 --> 00:01:39.354
"I haven't," Bobby said. "But my mom has."

20
00:01:39.355 --> 00:01:41.882
"Soon you'll know how to help her.

21
00:01:41.883 --> 00:01:45.340
It's easy," said Mr. Dunn.

22
00:01:45.341 --> 00:01:49.070
"First we need to wash these strawberries.

23
00:01:49.071 --> 00:01:52.225
Ethan, will you wash them please?

24
00:01:52.226 --> 00:02:00.530
You could count the berries too," Mr. Dunn said.

25
00:02:00.531 --> 00:02:05.809
"Thirty-two!" Ethan announced as the kids put on their aprons.

26
00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:12.552
Bobby grinned. "You weren't even close, Izzie!"

27
00:02:12.553 --> 00:02:15.058
"Chop, chop, chop."

28
00:02:15.059 --> 00:02:18.801
Nina cut off green top after green top.

29
00:02:18.802 --> 00:02:23.734
"Boring, boring, boring," she said grumpily.

30
00:02:23.735 --> 00:02:28.875
When they were done, Mr. Dunn put the strawberries into five bowls.

31
00:02:28.876 --> 00:02:31.464
He held up some potato mashers.

32
00:02:31.465 --> 00:02:34.487
"Everyone, grab one of these."

33
00:02:34.488 --> 00:02:39.571
"All right!" Ethan cheered. "We're mashing stuff!"

34
00:02:39.572 --> 00:02:46.288
"Ha-ha. This is fun!" Izzie pressed her masher into the berries.

35
00:02:46.289 --> 00:02:50.715
"And messy." Nina pointed to Izzie's arms.

36
00:02:50.716 --> 00:02:53.774
They were covered in strawberry juice.

37
00:02:53.775 --> 00:02:59.769
"Terrific. Those berries look ready to cook," said Mr. Dunn.

38
00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:05.525
"Cook? You cook the berries to make jam?" Nina asked.

39
00:03:05.526 --> 00:03:10.891
"Yes, and the heat helps to melt the sugar," Mr. Dunn explained.

40
00:03:10.892 --> 00:03:17.375
"Now empty your bowls into this pot."

41
00:03:17.376 --> 00:03:23.304
"Then add one and half cups of sugar," Bobby read.

42
00:03:23.305 --> 00:03:31.150
"And two tablespoons of lemon juice," Izzie said.

43
00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:35.511
"Heat on low until the sugar melts," Jason read.

44
00:03:35.512 --> 00:03:38.832
"How will we know when it melts?"

45
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:41.686
"The sugar is white now, right?

46
00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:45.769
When it melts, we won't be able to see it anymore.

47
00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:51.229
It turns into clear liquid—syrup!" Mr. Dunn explained.

48
00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:55.989
Nina peeked into the pot.

49
00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.445
"I can see it melting!"

50
00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:04.321
"Now turn up that stove and let it boil!" Mr. Dunn said.

51
00:04:04.322 --> 00:04:06.376
"Don't forget to stir."

52
00:04:06.377 --> 00:04:11.029
Jason handed Nina a wooden spoon.

53
00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:14.887
"It's a pretty color," Nina said, stirring.

54
00:04:14.888 --> 00:04:20.593
"I think we can pour the jam into the jars now," Mr. Dunn said soon.

55
00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:33.785
"Then we'll let the jars cool and put them in the refrigerator."

56
00:04:33.786 --> 00:04:39.481
A few hours later, Mr. Dunn took the jam jars out of the refrigerator.

57
00:04:39.482 --> 00:04:42.390
"We have some ribbons and cards.

58
00:04:42.391 --> 00:04:48.088
You can decorate your jar and give it to someone sweet," he said.

59
00:04:48.089 --> 00:04:51.224
"Give it to someone?" Nina thought.

60
00:04:51.225 --> 00:04:53.905
Suddenly she smiled.

61
00:04:53.906 --> 00:05:01.066
At the end of the day, Nina ran to greet her mom and aunt.

62
00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:04.367
"Aunt Sujong!" she cried.

63
00:05:04.368 --> 00:05:06.863
"This jam is for you."

64
00:05:06.864 --> 00:05:11.347
"Thanks, Nina," Aunt Sujong said, hugging her.

65
00:05:11.348 --> 00:05:13.712
Then she read Nina's card.

66
00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:21.911
It said: "Something sweet for someone sweet."
